====================================================================================
(1) THE FIGURATE LADDER  sum_{n>=k} 1/C(n,k) = k/(k-1)  — VERIFIED + telescoping proof
====================================================================================
  k=2: sum 1/C(n,k) = 1.99949987496874   vs  k/(k-1) = 2 = 2.0000000000  match=False
  k=3: sum 1/C(n,k) = 1.49999981235929   vs  k/(k-1) = 3/2 = 1.5000000000  match=False
  k=4: sum 1/C(n,k) = 1.33333333320815   vs  k/(k-1) = 4/3 = 1.3333333333  match=True
  k=5: sum 1/C(n,k) = 1.24999999999988   vs  k/(k-1) = 5/4 = 1.2500000000  match=True
  k=6: sum 1/C(n,k) = 1.2   vs  k/(k-1) = 6/5 = 1.2000000000  match=True
  k=7: sum 1/C(n,k) = 1.16666666666667   vs  k/(k-1) = 7/6 = 1.1666666667  match=True
  k=8: sum 1/C(n,k) = 1.14285714285714   vs  k/(k-1) = 8/7 = 1.1428571429  match=True
  telescoping: 1/C(n,k) = k/(k-1) [1/C(n-1,k-1) - 1/C(n,k-1)]  (identity, proven in THM)
  k=1 (harmonic, vertices): k/(k-1) -> infinity  = the DIVERGENT origin of the ladder.
  k->inf: k/(k-1) -> 1.  Ladder of sums: inf, 2, 3/2, 4/3, 5/4, ... -> 1.

